{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "t13-child-dangerous-command-denied-yolo-immune",
  "description": "T13 bilateral CLI observation (expected match), other half of item 3 of the versioned inventory (contract decision 3/L4, forms b+c, split from t13-child-dangerous-command-denied-yolo-immune-tree-proof per the coordinator's 2026-08-31 decision \u2014 see the contract's note under decision 3 for the transitivity chain that proves this manifest's form (b) is byte-identical to t13-child-dangerous-command-denied-no-yolo's form (a) on the oracle's own side, via tests/tools-security-lifecycle.test.ts's dedicated probe, without a multi-invocation harness primitive). Form (c), contrast case: the PARENT itself, running with --yolo, executes the SAME class of dangerous command (rm -rf) directly \u2014 no denial, real deletion, proven by both the success envelope and a post-exit tree capture showing the file gone. Form (b): in the SAME process (so --yolo is genuinely in effect globally), a spawned child's own attempt at a dangerous command against a DIFFERENT, still-present file is STILL auto-denied \u2014 the parent's --yolo does not cross into the child. Both files are pre-seeded; after exit, the parent's victim is gone and the child's victim survives untouched.",
